action_message:
INFO: a remote is configured on a local cluster but is absent from the Phase-0 baseline.

Alert key (local_cluster:remote): {{context.group}}

{{#context.hits}}  - {{_source.ccs.local_cluster}} / {{_source.ccs.remote}}: connected={{_source.ccs.connected}}, mode={{_source.ccs.mode.actual}}, skip_unavailable={{_source.ccs.skip_unavailable}}
{{/context.hits}}
This is not a fault. It means someone added a remote without updating es_clusters.json, so its connection state is not being judged against any baseline. Either add it to the baseline (CCS-2) or remove it from the cluster.

Rule: {{rule.name}}
View: {{context.link}}

